Patch 05 -- diagnostic native ARM bridge for the exact D3D8 AABB scan.

The current on-device guest/native profile attributes the hottest D3D8 block to
d3d8_mgs2_scan_aabb().  Patch 31 changed the algorithm and was withdrawn after
real play.  This candidate does not: range selection, validity checks and every
culling decision remain in Wine.  It replaces only the inner vertex walk with a
native ARM implementation using the same loads, isfinite rejection and float
min/max comparisons.

The bridge is gated by MGS2_BOX86_NATIVE_AABB=1, performs a native self-test
before publication, and recognises the companion noinline Wine build by an
exact 32-byte prologue.  Patch 04's complete-range protection check is reused.
The regparm=3 register arguments and four guest-stack arguments are copied
explicitly; the result is returned in guest EAX.

MGS2_GLIBC24_COMPAT is only for the retained local Ubuntu cross sysroot, whose
new libm symbol defaults otherwise raise the executable's requirement above the
handheld.  Normal/device-native builds leave it undefined.

NOT PRODUCTION. Built successfully as box86-native-aabb1, but a fixed-scene
device A/B is still required. The production launcher must keep this switch off
until screenshots, frame-time bands and the guest/native profile agree.

